Building on ideas in Nat Sothanaphan's recent note (arXiv:2512.14251), and motivated by Stijn's conjectures on extremal configurations for $6\mid n$ and for general even $n$, we can significantly improve the proven lower bound along even $n$. More precisely, we construct an explicit family of diameter-$2$ configurations for which\[
\liminf_{\substack{n\to\infty\\ n\ \mathrm{even}}}
\frac{\Delta(z_1,\dots,z_n)}{n^n}
\;\ge\;
\exp\!\left(\frac{7}{24}\zeta(3)-\frac{\pi^4}{864}\right)
\;\approx\;1.26853,
\]improving the previously proven constant $C\approx 1.0378$ from Sothanaphan's note.

I wrote up the details as a short note and uploaded the PDF (and tex) to my GitHub page ([here](https://github.com/QuanyuTang/counterexamples-problem-1045/blob/main/Another_improved_lower_bound_for_even_n.pdf)). With Stijn Cambie, Arne Decadt, Yanni Dong, and Tao Hu, we are preparing a full paper; this result will appear there in expanded form.

